WEBVTT

00:00:01.062 --> 00:00:07.814
Welcome to vNAAATS. This is FDD for Windows, the one fits all program for oceanic control.

00:00:09.222 --> 00:00:18.470
Controlling Oceanic means juggling a lot of tools. EuroScope, the flight data display. natTrak, CPDLC, controller calls and your audio client.

00:00:19.078 --> 00:00:23.494
D.D. for Windows brings them all together so you can control from one place.

00:00:24.262 --> 00:00:26.598
This is the flight data display in its own window.

00:00:26.918 --> 00:00:31.142
Every flight heading for the oceanic area is on your strips, grouped by track.

00:00:31.462 --> 00:00:33.158
each tango route as its own bridge.

00:00:33.702 --> 00:00:36.614
The alerts button takes you straight to any flight with a warning.

00:00:36.902 --> 00:00:41.350
and the aircraft menu has everything from tracking and transfers to a cell-cal check.

00:00:42.758 --> 00:00:46.086
natTrak, the VATSIM Oceanic Clearance System is built in.

00:00:46.438 --> 00:00:53.926
Pending and cleared lists show what needs your action, and natTrak opens in its own window that keeps your sign in, so you never leave the display.

00:00:55.398 --> 00:00:57.030
Your other tools sit along the top.

00:00:57.350 --> 00:01:05.958
The VACS button shows calls from other controllers. The audio chip shows who spoke last on your frequency. And CPDLC opens the data link window.

00:01:06.342 --> 00:01:14.694
clearance requests and level messages, which you can pop out onto another screen. One more thing we highly recommend using TrackAudio.

00:01:15.014 --> 00:01:22.438
you needed to get the full features of the vNAAATS flight data display, like who spoke last and the highlight on the aircraft that is transmitting.

00:01:23.750 --> 00:01:29.062
Beside it sits EuroScope. Pick an aircraft in EuroScope and it is highlighted in the display.

00:01:29.414 --> 00:01:33.574
commands such as track, release and transfer go from the display to the plugin.

00:01:35.238 --> 00:01:39.046
Play also works in a browser, and that is still the right choice on an iPad.

00:01:39.494 --> 00:01:41.286
but on Windows the app does much more.

00:01:41.606 --> 00:01:51.846
It starts EuroScope, VACS in your audio client for you. It keeps the plugin up to date and asks before it changes anything. It saves your key into the vnayats.cfg file.

00:01:52.102 --> 00:01:54.502
and brings that file up to date each time you open it.

00:01:54.950 --> 00:01:56.134
your own values.

00:01:56.454 --> 00:02:00.198
The program is already running, it leaves it alone so you never get a second copy.

00:02:00.742 --> 00:02:04.262
And you can paste your key just as it is, even with key equals in front.

00:02:04.518 --> 00:02:06.758
It has its own window and it updates itself.

00:02:07.750 --> 00:02:17.702
Getting started takes a few minutes. First, get your free API key at vnayats.com/get-key. Then download and install FDD for Windows and do the one-time setup.

00:02:18.054 --> 00:02:23.046
When you start the app it says, "Awaiting an active VATSIM connection." Connect in EuroScope.

00:02:23.334 --> 00:02:26.630
Within a few seconds the display opens on your position by itself.

00:02:27.750 --> 00:02:33.510
Here is how the install goes. Download the installer from vnaaats.com/windows and run it.

00:02:33.830 --> 00:02:41.990
You do not need administrator rights. The installer is not code signed yet. So if Windows Smart Screen says Windows protected your PC, just choose more info.

00:02:43.430 --> 00:02:45.318
The code signing page explains why.

00:02:46.662 --> 00:02:58.310
The first time you open the app, it walks you through a one-time setup. Choose your EuroScope folder, check the plugin, paste your key, and tick the programs you want it to open for you. After that, it opens straight to the display.

00:02:59.846 --> 00:03:02.662
FDD for Windows also looks after its own updates.

00:03:03.046 --> 00:03:11.430
FDD updates by itself, and when the app, the EuroScope plugin, the airline list, or the font needs updating, it prompts you and asks before it changes anything.

00:03:11.782 --> 00:03:16.294
Close your O-scope first then press update now. Your key is never touched.

00:03:17.190 --> 00:03:23.430
The key is personal, so keep it private. The display only opens while you are connected to VATSIM on an oceanic position.

00:03:23.878 --> 00:03:26.086
Remember, we highly recommend TrackAudio.

00:03:26.342 --> 00:03:32.957
Download FDD for Windows at vnayats.com/windows. One program, everything in one place.

